DSH Remote (https://github.com/liguobao/deepseek-harness-remote)
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 DSH Remote contributors

  The first phone link (protocol v1, now removed) adapted code from commit
  4d888ad of DSH Remote. Protocol v2 in link/ is written again in Rust, with
  its own frames, resumable links and reliable channel, and does not talk to
  DSH Remote. It keeps these parts of v1 that came from DSH Remote:
  - link/crates/core/src/keys.rs: the key pair, fingerprint and Base64URL
    functions of packages/crypto/src/index.ts.
  - link/crates/core/src/noise.rs: the Noise IK session and the remote-key
    check of packages/crypto/src/noise.ts.
  - link/crates/core/src/message.rs and frag.rs: the message envelope and
    the fragment layout of SecureMessageCodec in
    packages/protocol/src/index.ts.
  - link/crates/relay: the hello check, the device store, the heartbeat and
    the rate limits of apps/server/src/gateway.ts.
  - link/crates/host: the flow of HostServerConnection in
    packages/plugin/src/server-connection.ts (incoming links and the
    responder handshake).

  Full license text: the same MIT terms as printed under DeepSeek Harness
